    @classmethod
    def FlashHexFileWithControlFlow(cls, target, *args, session="default", **kwargs):
        'FlashHexFileWithControlFlow Method (fileName, controlFlow) Flash the contents of the hexfile to a target by using a specified control string. The hex file must be created using the method CreateHexFileForReferencePageAndCode() or CreateHexFileForWorkPageAndCode(). The controlFlow must be a string which contains the rules for flashing. The control string was typically build by the PROF toolbox in a user dialog. The controlFlow depends on the used target. A sample could be get by reading the target.log file after flashing with the tool. Getting the control flow: 1. Flash from the experiment. 2. To select a HEX file, choose “Hardware” - “Manage memory pages”. On the “Enhanced” tab, select the “Flash programming” action and apply it to “Data: ECU flash”. 3. Important: Select the desired flash parameters in Prof and flash the ECU. 4. Via the text editor, open the file under … ETAS\\LogFiles\\ProcessLogsV2\\TGTSVR.log 5. Look for the entry  StorePermanentlyToTarget . 6. For example, the following entry is displayed: “StorePermanentlyToTarget(KWP2000:1, C:\\APPLIK~1\\PROJEKTE\\MS6_\\P0516500.HEX seed2key 3 prog convert C:\\ETASDATA\\PROF2.1\\MS6\\ms6)” 7. Enter the parameters into the Tool-API command as follows: INVOKE (Device_ID, \'FlashHexFileWithControlFlow\', \'C:\\APPLIK~1\\PROJEKTE\\MS6_\\P0516500.HEX\', \'seed2key 3 prog convert C:\\ETASDATA\\PROF2.1\\MS6\\ms6\') - In the path of the HEX file, the DOS convention is not necessary. - In the path to the Prof control flow, the DOS convention is absolutely necessary, e.g. the path must not contain any spaces. Note on automatisation: The „PROF Control flow monitor“ must be closed manually at the end of the programming. (It is not possible to automatise this step). Workaround: change the  DEFAULT_SCREEN_LAYOUT (1) Mode  from 0 to 1 in the ProF-configuration The ProF-configuration is not allowed to contain the command "WAIT_FOR_KEY(-1)". This expects a manual key press. Parameters  fileName ( String )  describe the name and path for the file to create  controlFlow ( String )  describe how to flash a target.  Return Value  a boolean representing the success of the operation\nSource topic: Tool-API Verbindung aufbauen   / Experiment  / work with Experiment / Device  / Memory pages  / Flashen / FlashHexFileWithControlFlow'
        return Inca.invoke(target, 'FlashHexFileWithControlFlow', *args, session=session, **kwargs)

    @classmethod
    def FlashHexFileWithControlFlowOnFlashPort(cls, target, *args, session="default", **kwargs):
        'FlashHexFileWithControlFlowOnFlashPort Method (fileName, controlFlow, flashPort) Flash the contents of the hexfile to a target by using a specified control string. The hex file must be created using the method CreateHexFileForReferencePageAndCode() or CreateHexFileForWorkPageAndCode(). The controlFlow must be a string which contains the rules for flashing. The control string was typically build by the PROF toolbox in a user dialog. The controlFlow depends on the used target. A sample could be get by reading the target.log file after flashing with the tool. Getting the control flow: see description of FlashHexFileWithControlFlow(...) The additional parameter String flashPort must be a name of an available flash port (use GetSupportedFlashPortNames() to get them) The current flash port defined in the HWC is ignored when using this interface. This method is implemented for INCA 5.4. The method will not operate in former versions.  Getting the control flow: 1. Flash from the experiment. 2. To select a HEX file, choose “Hardware” - “Manage memory pages”. On the “Enhanced” tab, select the “Flash programming” action and apply it to “Data: ECU flash”. 3. Important: Select the desired flash parameters in Prof and flash the ECU. 4. Via the text editor, open the file under … ETAS\\LogFiles\\ProcessLogsV2\\TGTSVR.log 5. Look for the entry  StorePermanentlyToTarget . 6. For example, the following entry is displayed: “StorePermanentlyToTarget(KWP2000:1, C:\\APPLIK~1\\PROJEKTE\\MS6_\\P0516500.HEX seed2key 3 prog convert C:\\ETASDATA\\PROF2.1\\MS6\\ms6)” 7. Enter the parameters into the Tool-API command as follows: INVOKE (Device_ID, \'FlashHexFileWithControlFlow\', \'C:\\APPLIK~1\\PROJEKTE\\MS6_\\P0516500.HEX\', \'seed2key 3 prog convert C:\\ETASDATA\\PROF2.1\\MS6\\ms6\') - In the path of the HEX file, the DOS convention is not necessary. - In the path to the Prof control flow, the DOS convention is absolutely necessary, e.g. the path must not contain any spaces. Note on automatisation: The „PROF Control flow monitor“ must be closed manually at the end of the programming. (It is not possible to automatise this step). Workaround: change the  DEFAULT_SCREEN_LAYOUT (1) Mode  from 0 to 1 in the ProF-configuration The ProF-configuration is not allowed to contain the command "WAIT_FOR_KEY(-1)". This expects a manual key press. Parameters  fileName ( String )  describe the name and path for the file to create  controlFlow ( String )  describe how to flash a target.  flashPort ( String )  describe which flash port shall be used.  Return Value  a boolean representing the success of the operation\nSource topic: Tool-API Verbindung aufbauen   / Experiment  / work with Experiment / Device  / Memory pages  / Flashen / FlashHexFileWithControlFlowOnFlashPort '
        return Inca.invoke(target, 'FlashHexFileWithControlFlowOnFlashPort', *args, session=session, **kwargs)

