    @classmethod
    def RecorderAddDefaultComment(cls, target, *args, session="default", **kwargs):
        'GetOption Method (aParameterString) New interface INCA >= V7.2.3 to get current value(s) of an INCA option.  The desired option can be specified by using a parameter string with following structure:  "MODULE: aModuleName; OPTIONNAME: anOptionName"  Example: "MODULE: EXPERIMENT; OPTIONNAME: RecorderAddDefaultComment"  Some Module need additionally a DeviceName to get an option from desired device.  "MODULE: aModuleName; DEVICENAME: aDeviceName; OPTIONNAME: anOptionName"  Example: "MODULE: HWC; DEVICENAME: ETK test device:1; OPTIONNAME: BaudRate"  Remark: for most options it is mandatory that an Experiment is opened to get the option value.    Parameters  aParameterString ( String )  String containing the info which Option of which INCA module shall return its current value(s)  Return Value  Returned string will represent the value of the addressed option. If a value list shall be returned, a ; is used as separator.  If Option is not available or invalid ParameterStrig was sent, an API Error is returned.    SetOption Method (aParameterString) New interface INCA >= V7.2.3 to set / change the value of an INCA option.  The desired option can be specified by using a parameter string with following structure:  "MODULE: aModuleName; OPTIONNAME: anOptionName"; OPTIONVALUE: anOptionValue  Example: "MODULE: EXPERIMENT; OPTIONNAME: RecorderAddDefaultComment; OPTIONVALUE: true"  Remark: for most options it is mandatory that an Experiment is opened to get the option value.  Parameters  aParameterString ( String )  String containing the info which Option of which INCA module shall be changed by new value  Return Value  Returned true when action was done successful.  If Option is not available or invalid ParameterStrig was sent, an API Error is returned.\nSource topic: Tool-API Verbindung aufbauen   / Experiment  / work with Experiment / Recorder Configuration / Output File / RecorderAddDefaultComment'
        return Inca.invoke(target, 'RecorderAddDefaultComment', *args, session=session, **kwargs)

