    @classmethod
    def ReadASAP2FileAndHexFile(cls, target, *args, session="default", **kwargs):
        'ReadASAP2FileAndHexFile Method (asap2FileName, hexFileName) Read an Asap2 file and a HEX file and create an Asap2 project with a dataset. If the address ranges of the HEX file don\'t fit to the Asap2 file the asap2 project will be generated but without a dataset. HEX file without code: Reading a HEX file without code depends on the global Inca user option "Check dataset code". If set to "Yes" only HEX files containing code and data will create a dataset. If set to "No" also HEX files without code will create a dataset. The created Asap2 project has the same name as the Asap2 file without file extension. If an Asap2 project with this name is already available an index will be appended to it.  Parameters  asap2FileName ( String )  The full path name of the Asap2 file to be read The full path name consists of "Drive Nr"\\"Folder Hierarchy"\\"Asap2FileName"  hexFileName ( String )  The full path name of the HEX file to be read. The full path name consists of "Drive Nr"\\"Folder Hierarchy"\\"HEXFileName"  Return Value  The new created Asap2 project or null if an error occurs Possible reasons for an error: No space left on the drive containing the database. Invalid file name specified.\nSource topic: Tool-API Verbindung aufbauen   / - Database\n- Folder\n- Elements / Items / Project\n(A2L-file)  / ReadASAP2FileAndHexFile'
        return Inca.invoke(target, 'ReadASAP2FileAndHexFile', *args, session=session, **kwargs)

    @classmethod
    def ReadODXProject(cls, target, *args, session="default", **kwargs):
        'ReadODXProject Method (fileNames) Read an odx file and create an Asap2 project for this in the Inca database  Parameters  fileNames (array< String >[]()[][])  The full path name of the odx file to be read The full path name consists of "Drive Nr"\\"Folder Hierarchy"\\"odxFileName"  Return Value  The new created Asap2 project or null if an error occurs Possible reasons for an error: A database item with the specified name already exists. No space left on the drive containing the database. Invalid file name specified.\nSource topic: Tool-API Verbindung aufbauen   / - Database\n- Folder\n- Elements / Items / Read other description files / ReadODXProject '
        return Inca.invoke(target, 'ReadODXProject', *args, session=session, **kwargs)

    @classmethod
    def SetProject(cls, target, *args, session="default", **kwargs):
        'SetProject Method (prj) Set the project to the receiver. Setting a project to the receiver is a prerequisite to be able to work with this device. The method will force a commit for the database (if autocommit enabled)  Parameters  prj ( Asap2Project )  The project to be set. Usually an Asap2Project is used.  Return Value  boolean true or false depending on success of this method\nSource topic: Tool-API Verbindung aufbauen   / - Database\n- Folder\n- Elements / Items / Workspace / General / SetProject'
        return Inca.invoke(target, 'SetProject', *args, session=session, **kwargs)

    @classmethod
    def SetStatusOfKeyVariablesListNamed(cls, target, *args, session="default", **kwargs):
        'SetStatusOfKeyVariablesListNamed Method (aKeyVaiablesListName, aPropertyId) Set the current status of Key-Variables-List named by aKeyVaiablesListName to aPropertyId.  The propertyId shall be one of following:  ApplyNever  ... the KVL is never applied  ApplyOnOpeningEmptyEE  ... the KVL is applied when an empty EE is opened  ApplyOnOpeningExistingEE  ... the KVL is applied when an exising EE is opened  ApplyOnOpeningEE  ... the KVL is always applied when an EE is opened  Parameters  aKeyVaiablesListName ( String )  Name of key-variables-list for which the state should be returned  aPropertyId ( String )  String representation (propertyId) of the state to be set  Return Value  bool for success / no success\nSource topic: Tool-API Verbindung aufbauen   / - Database\n- Folder\n- Elements / Items / Project\n(A2L-file)  / KeyVariablesList / SetStatusOfKeyVariablesListNamed '
        return Inca.invoke(target, 'SetStatusOfKeyVariablesListNamed', *args, session=session, **kwargs)

